#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_trig_series

#% text
# `fourier_trig_series(f, t, k)` gives the trigonometric Fourier series of `f` to order `k`: `a_0/2` plus `a_n cos(n t) + b_n sin(n t)` for `n` from 1 to `k`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The coefficients are taken over the whole period: `a_n` is `1/pi` times the integral of `f cos(n t)` and `b_n` that of `f sin(n t)` over `[-pi, pi]`; `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` scales the frequency by `b`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_trig_series(t^2, t, 2)
#% output
#= cos(2*t) - 4*cos(t) + (1/3)*pi^2

#% cell
fourier_trig_series(t + t^2, t, 2)
#% output
#= cos(2*t) - 4*cos(t) - sin(2*t) + (1/3)*pi^2 + 2*sin(t)

#% section
# See also

#% text
